Error [E2304]: an indexed or sliced piece can't be handed back as a view
  --> tests/ui/view_index_into_param.jet:5:22
    |
  5 |     return line.words[0]
    |                      ^^^
 Why: indexing or slicing builds a fresh, owned piece, so there's no longer-lived value for a view to point at — the piece would vanish the moment this function returns
 Fix: return the piece owned (drop `view`; the caller keeps its own copy), or hand back a whole field with `view` and let the caller index it
